1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,520
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:15,880
What is this place? Where am I?

3
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,640
Wherever it is, it's completely dark.

4
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,760
I can't even see my own body.

5
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:23,840
It hurts.

6
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,740
Which way is up? Which way is down?

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,760
Where am I supposed to go?

8
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,040
Someone help me.

9
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,340
What? Is that a way out?

10
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:44,260
No! No, stop!

11
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:47,460
Voice. Maka. It's Maka's voice.

12
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,880
Wait there! I'm coming!

13
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:51,820
Saul!

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,660
Saul! Saul!

15
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,180
What's the matter?

16
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:10,600
Good, Dr. Medusa! It's Saul!

17
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:11,440
Ah!

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:17,500
Saul.

19
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,140
I'm all right.

20
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:23,960
I'll be okay.

21
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,500
I just had a bad dream, that's all.

22
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,980
That's good, Saul.

23
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:33,500
But if anything does come up, call me right away.

24
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,760
Ragnarok's black blood is mixed in with Soul Eaters.

25
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:44,480
It looks like I may have found myself a new research subject.

26
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,180
Listen to me.

27
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,360
He hosts the lyrics.

28
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:48,260
Let's see that in the air.

29
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,160
I'd love you.

30
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:49,400
I'd love you.

31
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,360
Thank you.

32
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:51,020
So, I'm...

33
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:51,740
See...

34
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:56,580
there you go.

35
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:57,200
Sweet Quaker!

36
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:59,160
ok

37
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:04,360
Super great to see the dialogue here.

38
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,220
Had a secret subcrow telling the audience for a while.

39
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,100
Ted's coming up throughivol faci the fire sestue.

40
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,040
nggak

41
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:13,720
Do you hear the sounds?

42
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:32,260
lo-okuninите-muna- Shaun

43
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:34,880
Yogi sei moakarose

44
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:38,380
demunyioro ho haji saat

45
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:47,560
didn't keep the way

46
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:53,160
that any of you

47
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:54,960
were

48
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:55,120
hoping

49
00:02:55,120 --> 00:03:02,160
away

50
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:19,440
All right, then, Sol.

51
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,460
I'm going to head home.

52
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,980
Unless you need something, are you thirsty?

53
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:25,960
Do you want me to get you a drink before I go?

54
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,680
No, don't worry about it.

55
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:29,380
What goes in must come out.

56
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:32,560
And I'm not too crazy about taking a leak in these stupid bedpans.

57
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:33,520
Okay.

58
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:38,520
Do you want me to bring you anything when I come back besides a change of underwear?

59
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:39,400
Hmm.

60
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,120
Nope, I can't think of anything.

61
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,160
Okay.

62
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:50,200
Hey, Maka, I'm in this bed because of something I did, not because of you.

63
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:52,280
So don't get yourself all worked up about it, okay?

64
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:55,380
Sorry.

65
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:02,960
Crap.

66
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:04,840
I think I just made her feel worse.

67
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,140
Way to go, Sol.

68
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,860
I'm an idiot letting my emotions show like that.

69
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:15,060
It's not going to do any good to get Sol worried about me.

70
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:17,820
Papa?

71
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,140
Come up to the roof with me.

72
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:21,560
We can watch the sunset.

73
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:25,040
Well, I'm here.

74
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,320
What am I supposed to do now?

75
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,040
Clean.

76
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,080
Put the library back in order.

77
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:29,620
Huh?

78
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,200
No way, not me.

79
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,180
Listen, you brat.

80
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:35,240
On your last extracurricular lesson, you didn't collect a single soul.

81
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:38,340
Yeah, well, that's what remedial lessons are for, right?

82
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,220
I should know I've done enough of them lately.

83
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,920
What will stacking books do me?

84
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:43,980
Cleaning?

85
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:45,100
No way.

86
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,320
I'm too big for that.

87
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:47,700
Stars don't clean.

88
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:52,020
Isn't there anything better for me to do, like when we beat up you and the crazy professor?

89
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,800
Listen up for once, Black Star.

90
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:57,460
You have more raw power than almost anyone else in your class.

91
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,660
And yet you have nothing to show for it.

92
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:01,000
It isn't fair to Tsubaki.

93
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,900
She's trying hard and you're holding her back.

94
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:05,080
Right now, what you need is punishment.

95
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:08,120
Something tedious and boring to get you back on track.

96
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:09,920
This is a huge mess.

97
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,140
Aren't you at least going to help me?

98
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:12,640
That would defeat the purpose.

99
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,460
I don't spoil my students.

100
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,380
That's not the kind of man I was.

101
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:19,140
Great.

102
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,320
What am I going to do now?

103
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:26,260
Charisma Justice is awesome.

104
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,480
He's almost as big a star as I am.

105
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,900
I never knew they had comic books in the library.

106
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:34,400
This is the kind of remedial lesson that I can live with.

107
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:35,740
Hey, keep it down, would you?

108
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,140
You're in a library.

109
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:38,780
Yeah, sorry.

110
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,960
What are you doing here, kid?

111
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,400
Are you being punished, too?

112
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:44,960
No, I'm here to check out a book.

113
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:48,000
I'm conducting some research into the symmetry of famous weapons.

114
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:50,560
I'd actually like to take that book that's under your butt,

115
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:51,940
if you don't mind moving for a second.

116
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,020
Oh, right here?

117
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,020
What does the cover say?

118
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:00,720
E-ex-calibur?

119
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:02,980
Almost. Excalibur.

120
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:04,080
Yeah, what's that?

121
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:06,580
From what I've heard, it's a legendary weapon,

122
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,000
also known as the Holy Sword.

123
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,180
They say he who draws the Holy Sword from the ground

124
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:12,100
will be deemed a hero

125
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:14,220
and shall receive everlasting glory and fame.

126
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:17,480
I've heard that someone who obtained Excalibur in the past

127
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,000
went on to become a mighty king.

128
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,960
I'll bet a sword as powerful as this one

129
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:23,620
has absolutely flawless symmetry.

130
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:24,920
Oh, symmetry.

131
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:25,760
Hero?

132
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:26,400
King?

133
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:27,900
That sounds perfect to me.

134
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,180
Oh, you mean Excalibur, huh?

135
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:31,180
Hey, Professor.

136
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:32,580
Are you here for punishment, too?

137
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:33,280
Punishment?

138
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,900
What are you talking about, Black Star?

139
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:37,440
Do you know anything about the Legend of Excalibur?

140
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,740
The Holy Sword Excalibur.

141
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:42,440
It was too much even for me.

142
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:43,420
Really?

143
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,820
You tried to pull the sword?

144
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:46,600
Even you couldn't draw the sword, Professor?

145
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:49,660
The Holy Sword Excalibur.

146
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,360
Now I'm really interested.

147
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:57,280
Legend of the Holy Sword.

148
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,500
Kid and Black Star's great adventure?

149
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,720
Look at that marker.

150
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,360
You see how ridiculous the sun looks

151
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,540
trying to fight off sleep?

152
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,420
Pretty funny.

153
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:12,740
This isn't going well at all.

154
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,820
I finally have a chance to talk to Maka,

155
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,580
and I don't have a clue what to talk about.

156
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:19,260
The way the sun looks is a pretty lame topic.

157
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,040
She pulled out a book.

158
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,360
She's bored with me.

159
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,480
I have to say something quick.

160
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:26,140
Something cleverer, something funny.

161
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:27,040
Think, think.

162
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:28,680
Think faster, idiot.

163
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:32,260
Hey, you shouldn't be reading in this light.

164
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:33,280
It's bad for your eyes.

165
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:35,600
Really?

166
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,880
Did I just start off by lecturing her?

167
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:41,780
Hey, Papa.

168
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:47,880
How do you feel about Mama?

169
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:48,560
Be honest.

170
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,860
Don't show any hesitation.

171
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,280
That's easy.

172
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:53,260
I love her, of course.

173
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:55,600
Then how come you cheated on her all the time?

174
00:07:55,600 --> 00:08:11,140
That was way too much hesitation.

175
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:13,440
Now, no matter what I say, it looks out convincing.

176
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:14,880
I'm in big trouble.

177
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:16,100
Hang in there.

178
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:18,360
Millions of men everywhere are on your side.

179
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,120
Don't run away from this.

180
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,220
Stand and face your daughter like a man.

181
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:23,060
Don't run.

182
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:23,820
Don't run.

183
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:24,560
Don't run.

184
00:08:24,780 --> 00:08:25,360
Don't run.

185
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:27,420
It's getting chilly, don't you think?

186
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,360
Maybe we should head inside, huh?

187
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:29,780
Already?

188
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:31,320
But we just got here.

189
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,160
I didn't run away quick enough!

190
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:34,920
All these pointed questions.

191
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:36,740
She's starting to take after her mother.

192
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:38,340
Listen, Maka.

193
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:41,460
Papa loves you and Mama more than anything in the world.

194
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:42,940
And that's the truth.

195
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,220
That's the truth.

196
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,240
It is the truth.

197
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:49,160
I swear it's the truth, Maka!

198
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:54,920
This is it.

199
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:55,760
Yahoo!

200
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:58,560
Excalibur's up there waiting for me.

201
00:08:58,740 --> 00:08:59,160
Yes.

202
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:02,880
According to this, we'll have to climb up there and find the cave the sword is in.

203
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:12,920
Hey!

204
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:13,940
Not there!

205
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:16,280
Dammit!

206
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:18,780
Squirled rich kids have all the best toys, don't they?

207
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:20,700
You're not leaving me behind!

208
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:30,960
Kid's not here.

209
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:31,640
Where'd he go?

210
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,240
In there, maybe?

211
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:34,640
Black Star?

212
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:35,580
Huh?

213
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:37,340
I can't come down.

214
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:37,840
There's water.

215
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:39,820
My pants are going to get wet.

216
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:41,320
What are you talking about?

217
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:42,500
You carry me.

218
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,360
Yeah, right.

219
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,680
You can stay there.

220
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:47,460
Such a terrible obstacle so early in the quest.

221
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:50,660
Our chosen path is truly a cruel one.

222
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,160
Yeah, you've really got it rough here, don't you?

223
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:57,480
I'll ward off the water from above and you can handle the water on the ground, okay?

224
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:58,660
We'll work together.

225
00:09:58,780 --> 00:10:00,140
It's a good thing there are two of us here.

226
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,840
This way would be impassable alone.

227
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:03,380
Quite an obstacle.

228
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,660
Dude, you're kind of a useless idiot, aren't you?

229
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:12,560
It looks like a fairy.

230
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:14,620
What's something like that doing here?

231
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,700
We're hunting after a legendary sword.

232
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:18,980
Finding a fairy or two shouldn't be surprising.

233
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:21,080
Is Excalibur up ahead?

234
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:22,280
Are we in the right place?

235
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:30,180
She's not a very polite fairy, is she?

236
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,500
Looks like the path dead ends here.

237
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,500
Hey, over there.

238
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:41,040
Yes, no doubt about it.

239
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,140
That's it.

240
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:44,500
The Holy Sword Excalibur.

241
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:49,340
Awesome.

242
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:51,360
The air here is vibrating.

243
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:57,460
Standing here, I can easily believe what the book says about becoming a hero and earning everlasting fame and glory.

244
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,800
This cave certainly seems like a magical place.

245
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,680
Just look at the sword.

246
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:06,700
Such precise, detailed ornamentation on the hilt and not a single nick on the blade.

247
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:09,960
This is indeed deserving of the title Holy Sword.

248
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:13,820
A magnificent sword which can only be pulled out by the chosen hero.

249
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,500
By me.

250
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:20,720
Yeah, looks like I'm a hero.

251
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,140
No, it can't be.

252
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:24,120
This is some kind of mistake.

253
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:26,000
I hate to break it to you, but you're no hero.

254
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,940
How about a do-over?

255
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:28,360
Huh?

256
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:30,240
You saying that didn't count or something?

257
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:33,500
Fine, but I'm sure it's just going to be the same every time.

258
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:35,880
No, this time I'm going to do it.

259
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,100
Yeah, right, you wish.

260
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:39,320
The sword chose me to be its hero, kid.

261
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,640
I'm a big, fat hero.

262
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:50,480
Best to be safe.

263
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,580
Who knows who else has touched this sword over the years.

264
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:53,680
Hurry up and do it.

265
00:11:53,680 --> 00:12:05,060
It came out, huh?

266
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:07,540
How come you were able to get it out, too?

267
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,220
It must be because I loosened it.

268
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:10,340
Welcome.

269
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:13,060
Welcome to my cave, young ones.

270
00:12:13,060 --> 00:12:17,680
It's talking.

271
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:20,480
Please forgive the belated salutations.

272
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:23,520
I am the holy sword, Excalibur.

273
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:36,520
How incredibly...

274
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:38,320
Lame!

275
00:12:38,320 --> 00:13:06,900
Papa, would you tell me more about the demon sword, Ragnarok?

276
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:17,560
Long ago, Meisters and Weapons worked together under Lord Death to maintain peace and order in the world,

277
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,940
the same function for which you are being trained.

278
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:25,820
No Meister and Weapon pair was allowed to collect the soul of a human being for any reason whatsoever.

279
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:31,220
That rule still stands, and now it seems as natural to us as breathing.

280
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:38,380
Because while a human soul increases a weapon's ability and power, just as a Kishan soul does, the price is steep.

281
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:43,340
A weapon that takes a human soul will pay by losing his or her own human heart.

282
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:51,660
Despite the risk, however, there were Meisters who broke that sacred rule.

283
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:54,560
These Meisters feared death above all else.

284
00:13:55,080 --> 00:14:00,060
Their constant battles left them frightened, broken, and they took to hunting human souls.

285
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:07,020
Again and again, they defied the rule, secretly feeding their weapons the souls of innocent humans.

286
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:14,020
As a result, a Kishan was born into this world.

287
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:21,020
Death Weapon Meister Academy was founded in order to recover souls who have left the human path and become eggs of Kishan.

288
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:28,020
It was also created to train and oversee Meisters and Weapons who are too young to hunt down evil without someone to guide them.

289
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:35,020
The ultimate goal is to prevent the Kishan from ever being reborn and once again raining terror down upon the world.

290
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:37,020
So, the demon sword...

291
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:40,020
Yes. It devours human souls.

292
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:44,020
It was melted down by a witch and implanted in the body of a Meister as black blood.

293
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:50,020
Now, the demon sword, Ragnarok, is only one step away from becoming a Kishan.

294
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:55,020
And it's not just the sword we have to worry about.

295
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:58,020
There are people who could become Kishan as well.

296
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:05,020
And beyond that, there's Soul, whose body now contains black blood.

297
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:12,020
Let's see. Are you still hard at work like a good boy black star?

298
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:15,020
Ooh, see what you can do if you put your mind to it?

299
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:19,020
Oh, hi, Professor Sid. After I put this book away, I'll be all done.

300
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:24,020
Tsubaki? So that sneaky little brat dumped his punishment on her and took off, did he?

301
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:27,020
Back when I was still alive, I hated it when dirty tricks like this were pulled.

302
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:31,020
It's okay, Professor. Don't worry about it. I enjoy cleaning.

303
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:35,020
If you're looking for black star, he's not here. He and Kid went to find the holy sword.

304
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:37,020
Why, has he done something wrong?

305
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:39,020
The holy sword?

306
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:41,020
Yes. Excalibur.

307
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:46,020
The same sword that tears the air and shakes the very ground?

308
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:52,020
Let's stop talking about it.

309
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:56,020
Yeah. In some way, this is the ultimate remedial lesson.

310
00:15:56,020 --> 00:16:00,020
I'll let this one slide. That's the kind of man I was.

311
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:04,020
Okay. I've got a bunch of tests that need greeting.

312
00:16:04,020 --> 00:16:14,020
You're the holy sword? In the top hat? Seriously?

313
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:18,020
You're one to talk in that funny outfit. Who are you exactly?

314
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:20,020
Who am I? I'm Blackstar!

315
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:23,020
My legend dates back to the 12th century, thank you very much.

316
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:26,020
From the looks of you, you must be meisters. Where are your children from?

317
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:29,020
Who do you think you are pointing that thing at me? Put it down, freak!

318
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:32,020
We're from death, we're in mine. I know that. Here, I want to show you something.

319
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:35,020
Then why did you ask if you already knew the answer?

320
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:38,020
What's with this guy? Why the hell isn't he wearing any pants?

321
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:40,020
What's he showing us, I wonder?

322
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:42,020
Young ones, do you want to hear the legend of me?

323
00:16:42,020 --> 00:16:43,020
Put that thing away!

324
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:45,020
Do you want to hear a heroic tale?

325
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:47,020
Get that out of my face!

326
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:48,020
Where have you traveled here from?

327
00:16:48,020 --> 00:16:51,020
Like we said, we're from Death Weapon Meister.

328
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:53,020
What is your favorite number between 1 and 12?

329
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:55,020
What? Between 1 and 12?

330
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:59,020
1, obviously, because I refuse to back down until I'm number 1.

331
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:02,020
And mine is 8 because of its perfect symmetry.

332
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:04,020
Hools! What right do you have to choose a number?

333
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:08,020
My legend dates all the way back to the 12th century, you know.

334
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:10,020
You asked us to pick a favorite number, so we did.

335
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:12,020
Do you want to hear my legend or not?

336
00:17:12,020 --> 00:17:15,020
Just quit with the cane already, will ya?

337
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:19,020
As I said, my legend begins in the 12th century.

338
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:23,020
My mornings begin with a cup of coffee with cream at the cafe.

339
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:29,020
My afternoons begin with a cup of hot tea with two lumps of sugar.

340
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:31,020
And my evenings...

341
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:33,020
Let me guess, booze.

342
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:35,020
Sounds right for an old guy like you.

343
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:38,020
In the evening, I change into my pajamas.

344
00:17:38,020 --> 00:17:40,020
Why do we care about that?

345
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:42,020
That's all irrelevant to the legend.

346
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:43,020
The seven ages.

347
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:45,020
Do you know what this hat is?

348
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:46,020
Huh?

349
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:48,020
I asked, do you know what this hat is?

350
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:49,020
How should we know that?

351
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:52,020
It appears to be made of silk, if that's what you mean.

352
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:53,020
Fools!

353
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:55,020
If you don't know, I guess I'll have to tell you.

354
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:58,020
The taller the chef's hat, the greater the chef.

355
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:00,020
Okay, so what you're trying to tell us then...

356
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:02,020
Who said that I was a chef?

357
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:04,020
Dude, nothing you're saying makes any sense.

358
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:07,020
This is why I can't abide hayseeds.

359
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:10,020
You're beyond annoying!

360
00:18:10,020 --> 00:18:11,020
Blackstar, calm down.

361
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:14,020
Don't let this guy and his nonsense get to you.

362
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:16,020
Holy sword, you gotta be kidding me!

363
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:17,020
Let me see that book!

364
00:18:17,020 --> 00:18:18,020
It's completely unreliable!

365
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:19,020
Who wrote this?

366
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,020
Let's see.

367
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:21,020
The author is...

368
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:25,020
E. Excalibur?

369
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,020
Excalibur.

370
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:27,020
It was you!

371
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:28,020
No autographs.

372
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:32,020
Professor, I have a question.

373
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:35,020
What kind of weapon is the holy sword?

374
00:18:35,020 --> 00:18:36,020
Oh.

375
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:37,020
That, huh?

376
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:42,020
Whoever draws the sword is said to be made a great king, given wings of light and granted

377
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:44,020
the ability to soar through the sky.

378
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:47,020
The sword can cut through space with a single swing.

379
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:50,020
Without a doubt, it is the most powerful weapon in the world.

380
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:51,020
I see.

381
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:56,020
But only a hero who's been chosen can match soul wavelengths with it, right?

382
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:57,020
Hmm.

383
00:18:57,020 --> 00:18:58,020
No.

384
00:18:58,020 --> 00:19:00,020
That's not true, unfortunately.

385
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:03,020
Surprisingly enough, Excalibur can match with anyone.

386
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:09,020
Before becoming my Meister, there is a list of a thousand provisions you must peruse.

387
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,020
Be sure to look through all of them.

388
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,020
They're important.

389
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:14,020
Even the backs of these pages have been written on.

390
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:20,020
I greatly look forward to your participation in number 452, the five-hour storytelling party.

391
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,020
And thus...

392
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:26,020
Thus you have been chosen.

393
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:29,020
It shall all be yours.

394
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:31,020
Victory and glory.

395
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:32,020
Victory.

396
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:33,020
Glory.

397
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:36,020
Now let's go.

398
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,020
Together.

399
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:38,020
Together.

400
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:39,020
Yeah, right.

401
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:40,020
Who'd ever want a sword like you?

402
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:41,020
Useless piece of metal.

403
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:42,020
Anybody can match their soul wavelength with the sword just fine.

404
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:56,020
But there's no one in the world who can ever match personal wavelengths with Excalibur.

405
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:57,020
Babe.

406
00:19:57,020 --> 00:19:58,020
Hold on.

407
00:19:58,020 --> 00:19:59,020
Come back.

408
00:19:59,020 --> 00:20:00,020
I tell you what.

409
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:03,020
I can lower those 1,000 provisions down to 800.

410
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:07,020
Just as long as you take part in this storytelling party.

411
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:10,020
Anyone who can put up with him is a hero.

412
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:11,020
Disgusting.

413
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:12,020
Oh, hi.

414
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:15,020
Did you meet the Holy Sword Excalibur?

415
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:36,020
Yeah, they met him.

416
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:40,020
We've both got fine partners already, huh?

417
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:41,020
Hmm?

418
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:43,020
All right.

419
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:45,020
It looks like the gang is all here.

420
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:46,020
Hey, So.

421
00:20:46,020 --> 00:20:48,020
So, are you all fixed up now?

422
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:51,020
The real party can't get started without you around.

423
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:52,020
Yeah.

424
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:53,020
I'm a lot better.

425
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,020
Do you hear that, Black Star?

426
00:20:56,020 --> 00:21:00,020
I'm starting to get the strange feeling that other people have been laughing at us.

427
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:01,020
Huh?

428
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:02,020
Those two?

429
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:03,020
They're the ones?

430
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,020
Yeah, it's for them.

431
00:21:06,020 --> 00:21:07,020
Hey, Black Star.

432
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:08,020
Kid, come here.

433
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:09,020
I think you better see this.

434
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:10,020
Hmm?

435
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:23,020
Is he serious?

436
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:26,020
What is that thing?

437
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:27,020
Don't know.

438
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:28,020
It's intense.

439
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:29,020
That freak!

440
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:30,020
Disgusting.

441
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:35,020
Huh?

442
00:21:35,020 --> 00:21:38,020
Not a dream or not.

443
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:40,020
Oh,?

444
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:42,020
What does it need for me to score?

445
00:21:42,020 --> 00:21:43,020
Oh, man.

446
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:45,020
How about it?

447
00:21:45,020 --> 00:21:46,020
Oh, but I dunno.

448
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:47,020
Yeah.

449
00:21:47,020 --> 00:21:48,020
How about it?

450
00:21:48,020 --> 00:21:49,020
Oh, man.

451
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:51,020
I'd rather the leap.

452
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:54,020
I'd rather the leap go.

453
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:56,020
The leap of the leap.

454
00:21:56,020 --> 00:22:26,000
See you next time.

455
00:22:26,020 --> 00:22:56,000
See you next time.

456
00:22:56,020 --> 00:22:58,020
I love it!

457
00:23:26,020 --> 00:23:30,440
In the next episode of Soul Eater, the enchanted sword Masamune, rake the soul possession.

458
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:31,920
A heart sings in the rain?

459
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:32,480
Fool!

460
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,920
You're so annoying!

